# M-NATIVE-01 — one-shot ARM64 diagnostic authorization (2026-10-25)

Test question: Can the pinned Collabora/LibreOffice native engine, the AquaWord
source overlay and Android Gradle packaging produce a structurally verified
arm64-v8a debug APK at this exact feature-branch commit?

Why source tests are insufficient: JVM snapshot/SAF simulations and desktop
DOCX round-trips cannot prove native C++ toolchain integration, ABI packaging,
Gradle resource/manifest linking or the actual Collabora Android build.

Scope: compile/package/ABI and SHA-256 checks only. No Android emulator
certification, device run, final release, auto-merge or main modification.
The runner may take hours and may fail due to disk/toolchain limits.
Only free GitHub-hosted runner resources are permitted.

Trigger safety: android-native.yml responds to the *addition* of this file
on fix/saf-save-failure-recovery-20261023. Editing this file or any other
subsequent push must NOT trigger another diagnostic build. The existing
manual workflow_dispatch path remains available for separately justified runs.

Acceptance reporting: record exact commit SHA, native workflow run URL,
PASS/FAIL/PENDING, APK architecture/manifest and SHA-256 only if actually
produced. Real Writer Arabic/English DOCX edit/save/reopen, Android SAF and
Xiaomi Pad 5 remain NOT TESTED until independent runtime evidence exists.
